            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Believers or groups of people in covenant relationship with God, deriving their spiritual life, sustenance, and fruitfulness from Christ or the covenant root.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"John 15:1-8\",\"Romans 11:16-24\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The Messiah (typically as the singular 'Branch' or 'Shoot'), representing the prophetic restoration of the Davidic royal line.\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 11:1\",\"Jeremiah 23:5\",\"Zechariah 3:8\",\"Zechariah 6:12\"],\"prominence\":\"dominant\"},{\"meaning\":\"Individuals or groups facing divine judgment and removal from the covenant (withered, broken, or burned branches).\",\"basis\":[\"John 15:6\",\"Romans 11:20-21\",\"Malachi 4:1\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Prosperity, expansion, and earthly blessing of a tribe or nation.\",\"basis\":[\"Genesis 49:22\",\"Psalm 80:10-11\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"In New Testament interpretation, the plural 'branches' universally symbolizes believers attached to Christ (the Vine) or Israel and Gentiles attached to God's covenant (the Olive Tree). In Old Testament prophecy, the singular 'Branch' is a major Messianic title.\"}",
